From 74f6659d81444d67dc18a6541cf1243d50c3bb29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@localhost>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:55:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: strip patch-header metadata from the WMT download
 address

Byte 24 of each MT8163 patch header carries the patch count in its high
nibble and the download sequence in its low nibble. The stock launcher
reads header[24..27] as one word, extracts both fields, then zeroes that
byte before passing the word to the kernel as the patch download address.

The driver had been sending the raw word, so the DLM patch was written to
0xf00e0021 and the ILM patch would have gone to 0x00060022: 0x21/0x22
bytes high and, worse, misaligned. r176 confirmed this on hardware. The
DLM body appeared at AP 0x5f6e0021 rather than 0x5f6e0000, the controller
faulted with an ABT exception, and R1 held 0xf00e0029, exactly eight bytes
into the misplaced body where the first structure begins.

Zero the metadata byte in both entries so the patches land at 0xf00e0000
and 0x00060000, and log the address actually programmed so a UART capture
can prove which constants the running image carries.

No firmware bytes, patch order, header skip, fragment size or flag, STP
sequencing, BTIF DMA behaviour, CONSYS power/timing, EMI mapping, DTB or
boot packaging changed.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
index a51f2c1..80147fe 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
@@ -833,6 +833,8 @@ static int mt8163_stp_download_patch(struct mt8163_stp *stp,
 	if (ret)
 		goto out;
 	memcpy(partial_address_cmd + 12, address, 4);
+	dev_info(stp->dev, "WMT patch %s download address %4ph\n", name,
+		 partial_address_cmd + 12);
 	ret = mt8163_stp_wmt_xfer(stp, partial_address_cmd,
 				  sizeof(partial_address_cmd), wmt_patch_address_evt,
 				  sizeof(wmt_patch_address_evt));
@@ -891,9 +893,18 @@ static int mt8163_stp_bootstrap(struct mt8163_stp *stp)
 		const char *name;
 		u8 address[4];
 	} patches[] = {
-		/* Stock launcher runs download sequence 1 before sequence 2. */
-		{ "mediatek/ROMv2_lm_patch_1_1_hdr.bin", { 0x21, 0x00, 0x0e, 0xf0 } },
-		{ "mediatek/ROMv2_lm_patch_1_0_hdr.bin", { 0x22, 0x00, 0x06, 0x00 } },
+		/*
+		 * Byte 24 of each patch header is metadata, not address: the
+		 * stock launcher reads header[24..27] as one word, derives the
+		 * patch count from its high nibble and the download sequence
+		 * from its low nibble, then clears that byte before handing the
+		 * word to the kernel as the download address. Sending it
+		 * verbatim placed each patch body 0x21/0x22 bytes high and
+		 * misaligned, which is what the controller aborted on.
+		 * Download sequence 1 still runs before sequence 2.
+		 */
+		{ "mediatek/ROMv2_lm_patch_1_1_hdr.bin", { 0x00, 0x00, 0x0e, 0xf0 } },
+		{ "mediatek/ROMv2_lm_patch_1_0_hdr.bin", { 0x00, 0x00, 0x06, 0x00 } },
 	};
 	unsigned int i;
 	int ret;
-- 
